                <pb facs="0811" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/>

                <head>Accident to President Roosevelt.</head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Telegram from the minister for foreign
                        affairs of Japan to the Japanese Minister to the United States, left by
                        Count Mutsu, secretary of Japanese legation, at the Department of State,
                        September 6, 1902.</hi></p>
                <p>His Majesty, the Emperor, commands you to convey to the President his sincere
                    congratulations for the fortunate escape of the President from the consequences
                    of the accident which might have proved very serious, and also to express His
                    Majesty’s wishes for the continual health and welfare of the President.</p>

                <xi:include href="ch201/d725.xml" xpointer="d725"/>
            </div>
